  "body": "\r\nAllow bind others element's attribute without necessary javascript.\r\n```html\r\n<span>{{value}}</span>\r\n<input type=\"text\" value=\"{{value:input}}\">\r\n```\r\nBind object to template\r\n```html\r\n<template id=\"template1\">\r\n    <span>{{data.prop1}}</span>\r\n</template>\r\n<script>\r\n    document.querySelector('#template1').data = { prop1: 'prop1' };\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\nBind array to template\r\n```html\r\n<template id=\"template2\">\r\n    <span>{{data.0.prop1}}</span>\r\n</template>\r\n<script>\r\n    document.querySelector('#template2').data = [{prop1: 'prop1'}]\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\nBind computed property to template\r\n```html\r\n<template data=\"{{data}}\">\r\n    <span>{{data.fullName}}</span>\r\n</template>\r\n<script>\r\nconst data = {\r\n    firstName: 'first',\r\n    lastName: 'last',\r\n    get fullName() {\r\n        return `${this.firstName}  ${this.lastName}`;\r\n    },\r\n    set fullName(value) {\r\n        const [firstName,lastName] = value.split(' ');\r\n        this.firstName = firstName;\r\n        this.lastName = lastName;\r\n    },\r\n};\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\nOr just like polymer‘s data binding, any plans about that?\r\n",
